Eigenmath for generated9
=======================

This is the command-line Eigenmath computer algebra system by George Weigt.
It builds with the native Plan 9 compiler, libc and libbio, without APE,
NPE or a JavaScript runtime. See UPSTREAM for source revisions and licenses.

Build, test and install inside generated9:

    cd /sys/src/cmd/eigenmath
    mk
    mk test
    mk install

On amd64, use generated9's rebuilt 6c: the bootstrap compiler predates its
fix for floating-point comparisons involving NaN. See boot/README.md.

Run interactively in a rio window or on the serial console:

    eigenmath
    ? d(sin(x),x)
    ? integral(x^2,x)
    ? det(((a,b),(c,d)))
    ? exit

The question mark is the prompt, not part of the input. Ctrl-D also exits.
Each interactive line is evaluated separately; use a script or redirected
input for multiline expressions. Lines are not truncated to 1000 bytes.

From rc:

    echo 'd(sin(x),x)' | eigenmath
    eigenmath examples/oscillator
    eigenmath < examples/oscillator

With no file arguments, Eigenmath reads standard input. A file argument of
"-" also reads standard input. Several files share one evaluation context;
execution stops at the first failed file. File arguments do not implicitly
start an interactive session afterward. run("filename") reads another script.
Scripts and redirected input retain upstream's 1,000,000-byte size limit.

Results go to standard output, errors to standard error. Evaluation and I/O
errors return a failing Plan 9 exit status. In interactive mode, an evaluation
error returns to the prompt; the session retains a failing exit status.

tty=1 selects linear text output; tty=0 restores two-dimensional formulas.
Like the upstream command-line front end, draw evaluates to nil and produces
no graph. The macOS/browser graphical front ends have not been ported.

mk test runs upstream's selftest, numeric boundary checks for the local math
routines, and native CLI regression tests. Additional upstream examples:

    6.out test/demotest
    6.out test/misctest

Use your architecture's executable prefix instead of 6 when appropriate.
Runtime validation has been performed on generated9/amd64.

Eigenmath documentation: https://georgeweigt.github.io/
